## TypeScript API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to provide a clear, intuitive, and extensible way for end-users (developers integrating with 3D scenes) to control camera animations in TypeScript, balancing simplicity with powerful customization.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing all animation logic. Instances represent individual cameras within a scene.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(camera: THREE.PerspectiveCamera, scene: THREE.Scene) {
           this.camera = camera;
           this.scene = scene;
           this.animationQueue = []; // Internal queue for scheduled animations
       }

       // Animation Definition & Scheduling
       static createAnimation(type: AnimationType, params: AnimationParameters): AnimationDefinition {
           // Factory method - returns a structured animation definition object
           //  (see details below)
       }

       addAnimation(definition: AnimationDefinition) {
           this.animationQueue.push(definition);
           // Internal logic to prioritize/schedule based on timing, dependencies, etc.
       }

       start() {
           this.animateLoop(); // Initiate continuous animation playback
       }
       private animateLoop() { /*  Handles frame updates, animation execution, and queue management */ }

       // Advanced Control
       pause(): void;
       resume(): void;
       clearQueue(): void;
       getCurrentAnimation(): AnimationDefinition | null; 
   }
   ```

2. **`AnimationType` Enum:**  Defines fundamental animation styles:

   ```typescript
   enum AnimationType {
       LINEAR,  // Constant speed movement
        trayectoria, // Path-based (e.g., along a spline)
       ROTATION, // Smooth camera rotations
       FADE_IN_OUT, // Gradual appearance/disappearance (opacity changes)
       ZOOM,     // Perspective zoom adjustments
       CUSTOM    //  User-defined functions for complex behaviors
   }
   ```

3. **`AnimationParameters` Interface (Generic):**  Holds parameters *specific* to each `AnimationType`.

   ```typescript
   interface AnimationParameters {
       duration: number;  // Animation length in seconds
       easing: EasingFunction; //  (linear, easeIn, easeOut, custom)
       ... animaciónTypeSpecificProps

